Step 2 — Foundation Questions
What kind of work do I want to do?
I want to do work where I can solve problems, protect systems, analyze threats, and work with
technology. I want my work to involve more than just completing repetitive tasks. I would like to
investigate problems, find solutions, improve security, and eventually help lead a team or
organization.
Who do I want to serve or impact?
I want my work to help businesses, government organizations, employees, and everyday people
protect their information and technology. I am especially interested in helping organizations
prevent cyberattacks and keeping important information from falling into the wrong hands.
What values do I want my career to embody?
I want my career to represent:
>Integrity
>Responsibility
>Discipline
>Leadership
>Reliability
>Continuous improvement
>Service to others
What kind of professional do I want to become?
I want to become someone who is dependable, knowledgeable, calm under pressure, and able
to solve difficult problems. I also want to be known as someone who can lead people without
forgetting what it is like to be part of the team. I want coworkers and employers to trust me with
important responsibilities.
What does success look like for me — not financially, but meaningfully?
Success would mean having a career where I feel like my work actually matters. I want to know
that I am protecting people or organizations, solving important problems, and continuing to
improve myself. I would also like to eventually become a leader who can mentor others and help
them grow professionally.
